.TH CENTCOM-DOCTOR 1 "" "centcom 0.1.0 (contract 1.2.0)" "Centcom"
.SH NAME
centcom\-doctor \- check this computer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B centcom doctor [\-\-json] [\-\-bundle <file>] [\-\-cost [<transcript>...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Checks node, terminal, keychain, git, network, the relay, your sign\-in, the version and the clock. With \-\-cost it reports where a Claude Code session's tokens went and what Centcom adds to each turn (no model call).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-cost [<transcript>...]
report token use of recorded Claude Code transcripts, or the launch flags of a Centcom turn when none is named
